                <pb facs="0168" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg50"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 417.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Prince de Chimay to Mr. Tree.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 19,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Referring to your letter of the
                    6th of this month, I have the honor to inform your excellency that the man
                    Sambolino, Adolph, was conducted on board of the steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Westernland</hi>, Saturday, the 10th of November, and surrendered into the
                    hands of Mr. Heidelberg.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prince de Chimay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
